{% card "About", "intro" %}
  <p class="hi">Hi!</p>

  <p class="lede">
    I'm a PhD computer scientist, software engineer, homelabber, zerg player, content creator, biker, guitar player, husband, and a dad.
  </p>

  <p>
    These days I'm an Applied Scientist at <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/">Amazon Web Services</a>, on the
    <a href="https://github.com/strata-org/Strata">Strata</a> team in the Automated Reasoning Group.
    Strata is a verification platform with many front ends and back ends. I work on
    <a href="https://github.com/strata-org/Strata-Python">StrataPython</a>, its pipeline for verifying
    Python programs with contracts, where I design and develop an IR for formal verification of dynamic languages, along with its
    compiler and abstract interpretation passes.
  </p>

  <p>
    Before that, I did my PhD at <a href="https://sice.indiana.edu/">IU Bloomington</a> in compilers &amp;
    programming languages, with a minor in
    <a href="https://philosophy.indiana.edu/student-portal/graduate/minors/pure-and-applied-logic-certificate.html">logic</a>.
    My research focused on the run-time performance of production-grade, self-hosting languages on
    tracing JIT compiler back-ends (<a href="{{ site.links.dissertation }}">dissertation</a>). Along the way
    I spent about three years at <a href="https://canonical.com/">Canonical</a> on the
    <a href="https://github.com/juju">Juju</a> team, working on distributed orchestration at scale.
    I also hold an <a href="/cv/#edu-msc-bogazici">MSc</a> in computer engineering, focused on machine learning.
  </p>

